Why Is Demand Increasing
Advanced Node Complexity: Sub-7nm and increasingly complex semiconductor structures require highly sensitive inspection systems capable of identifying extremely small defects.
AI-Enabled Inspection: Artificial intelligence is improving automated defect classification and helping manufacturers reduce false positives while extracting more information from inspection data.
Advanced Packaging: Chiplets, heterogeneous integration, interposers, bonding, and through-silicon vias are creating new defect categories that require sophisticated inspection technologies.

Semiconductor Inspection Watch: Hybrid Optical and Electron-Beam Platforms
Inspection systems are evolving toward hybrid architectures that combine the speed of optical scanning with the resolution of electron-beam inspection. X-ray and other complementary technologies are also gaining importance as semiconductor manufacturing moves toward increasingly complex structures and advanced packaging.

