Why This Market Matters
Semiconductor defect inspection systems play a critical role in protecting wafer yield and device reliability by identifying particles, pattern distortions, structural flaws, and other manufacturing anomalies. As semiconductor geometries shrink and packaging architectures become more complex, inspection accuracy, throughput, and automated defect classification are becoming increasingly important.

